{"ts": "2026-10-21T07:29:17.220716Z", "run_id": "r-20261021T0729Z-ec22", "unit": "kiro:cross-tenant-copy", "seq": 8, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-004", "target": "C-3affbf7d", "decision": "reject", "by": "human", "reason": "R3.2 is not implemented. _select (packages/core/src/mintmory/core/transfer.py:72-109) never compares the remaining filter/all_active rows with COPY_MAX; the only cap check is len(plan) at :247, after duplicates are skipped, which is R3.4's rule (records to copy). test_skipped_duplicates_do_not_count_toward_copy_max (packages/core/tests/test_transfer_selection.py) encodes the wrong rule: all_active with COPY_MAX=2 over 3 active rows must raise under R3.2; keep R3.4's point there with a selection that passes R3.2 (rows <= COPY_MAX) and a duplicate skipped. WHEN all_active or a filter selects more than COPY_MAX non-superseded rows in the source tenant, even if some of them are duplicates in the destination THEN copy_between_tenants raises CopySelectionError(\"selection exceeds {COPY_MAX} memories\") before any write and the destination is unchanged", "text_sha256": "a166c15d6d0b572286c76c6f219e822dcfe78b43d9506f1e41e00bb36eaef8ba", "answer_sha256": "26c19ec28867c400aebb431ddcb8ef117f22434a794bee4fcd089288a2b4bba1"}
